    {
      "note": "OntoUML has no way to add a member to a generalization set while omitting only the OWL disjointness, so the pitfall is modelled as a second, non-disjoint generalization set {Tiger} with the same categorizer. Under the profile rule (disjoint+complete -> gufo:partitions, otherwise gufo:categorizes) that set yields gufo:categorizes. Upstream states only gufo:partitions. The extra triple is entailment-neutral for the pitfall (gufo:partitions already implies the categorization), and it is not what the rule OG-UFO-PARTITION-DISJOINT or gufoshapes detect. Pending NEMO review of the OntoUML encoding of this pitfall.",
